From: fil-c-utils maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Disable x87 control-word assembly under Fil-C

Fil-C rejects the memory operands used by fnstcw and fldcw, leaving run-time
traps in gnulib's long-double printf paths. Fil-C's musl fenv implementation
does not expose a way to change the x87 precision control, so its default
extended precision remains in effect and the control-word save/restore is
unnecessary.

--- a/lib/fpucw.h
+++ b/lib/fpucw.h
@@ -65,7 +65,8 @@ extern "C" {
 
 
 /* Inline assembler like this works only with GNU C and clang.  */
-#if (defined __i386__ || defined __x86_64__) && (defined __GNUC__ || defined __clang__)
+#if !defined __FILC__ \
+    && (defined __i386__ || defined __x86_64__) && (defined __GNUC__ || defined __clang__)
 
 typedef unsigned short fpucw_t; /* glibc calls this fpu_control_t */
 
